          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பாலைவனம் (pālaivaṉam) is pālai, the dry wasteland of old Tamil poetry, named after a plant of that land (DEDR 4100), and vaṉam, \"forest, tract\", from Sanskrit vana (CDIAL 11258)."
